.TH SYS_PROC_THR_COUNT 2 "2026-05-13" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_proc_thr_count \- return the count of threads owned by a process
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_proc_thr_count(pid_t " pid ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_proc_thr_count ()
returns the number of threads currently owned by the process whose ID is
.IR pid .
If
.I pid
is 0, the current process is implied.
.PP
Use the returned count to size a buffer for
.BR sys_proc_thr_list (2):
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
int n = sys_proc_thr_count(pid);
sys_thrinfo_t *buf = malloc(n * sizeof(*buf));
sys_proc_thr_list(pid, buf, n * sizeof(*buf));
.fi
.RE
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success the non-negative thread count is returned.
On failure, a negated errno is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B ESRCH
.I pid
does not refer to an existing process.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_proc_thr_list (2),
.BR sys_proc_threads (2),
.BR sys_proc_info (2),
.BR thr_self (2)
